[0.25,"o","A Bluetooth headset intercom for Linux\r\n\r\nUsage: bt-intercom [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  scan         Scan for nearby Bluetooth devices\r\n  pair         Pair, trust, and connect a headset\r\n  remove       Remove a headset from the saved intercom network\r\n  status       Show Bluetooth headset audio status\r\n  diagnose     Test adapters and headsets on real hardware: connects them, exercises A2DP and HFP, and measures simultaneous SCO links per controller. Uses the saved network when no address is given. Stop any running intercom first: profiles are switched and restored to A2DP (unsaved)\r\n  run          Route configured headset microphones to one another, optionally showing the live dashboard\r\n  completions  Generate shell completion definitions\r\n  panel        Open the interactive terminal control panel\r\n  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n      --verbose  Enable detailed diagnostics on stderr (unless RUST_LOG is set)\r\n  -v, --version  \r\n  -h, --help     Print help\r\n\r\nQuick start (with two HFP/HSP headsets):\r\n  bt-intercom scan\r\n  bt-intercom pair ADDRESS\r\n  bt-intercom status ADDRESS_1 ADDRESS_2\r\n  bt-intercom run ADDRESS_1 ADDRESS_2\r\n\r\nRun `bt-intercom <command> --help` for options; `pair` and `panel` need an interactive terminal.\r\n"]
